# TEMPORARY (2026-09-28, until the HANDOFF.md queue is done): the LIGHT gate, `complete:light`.
# It keeps every static check (type-check, lint, both spec lints, format, the contract-bundle, docs and
# cross-repo checks) plus the unit and cross-cutting suites — nothing that starts `mongod`.
#
# Left out, so run the full `npm run complete` by hand before merging a lane and once on main after
# each merge (CI still runs all of it):
#
# - `test:integration`, `test:contract` and `test:fuzz` — the database and HTTP layers, fuzz being
#   most of the full gate's minutes;
# - `docs:build`.
#
# Restoring the full gate: revert the commit that introduced this block.
#
# `check:spec-identity` SKIPS rather than fails when the paired frontend is not on disk, so a
# half-cloned pair can still commit. It stays fatal under CI, where a missing sibling means the
# workflow is misconfigured.
#
# Deliberately not here, and run by hand for the occasions that want them: `test:mutation`
# (re-executes the unit suite once per mutant — nightly in CI), `complete:manual` (`test:prism`,
# which binds a real port), and `bench` / `bench:search` (need a running server, and report numbers
# rather than a verdict).
# Write the generated artefacts first, then verify them. Regenerating here rather than leaving it
# to whoever remembers is what stops a commit failing the gate with "STALE" for a file no human
# authors. Costs about five seconds for the contract artefacts.
#
# `--no-sync` is not optional. A full `regenerate` ends with `sync:frontend`, which writes into the
# PAIRED REPO's working tree — a commit here would silently dirty a checkout you are not looking
# at, and possibly one with its own work in progress. Hand the files over deliberately, with
# `npm run regenerate` by itself, when you mean to.
#
# `git add` is required for what's still committed: a file rewritten after staging is not in the
# commit, so the gate below would pass against content that is not what gets committed. Note this
# widens a partial `git add -p` to include the whole regenerated output — which is what you want
# for a generated file, and a surprise exactly once.
#
# `openapi.yaml`, `api/` and `src/types/asyncapi.generated.ts` are NOT
# named here — they are gitignored (postinstall rebuilds them, see package.json), and `git add`
# errors outright on an explicitly-named ignored path. `regenerate` above still has to build them:
# the gate that follows reads them off disk regardless of git's opinion of them.
npm run regenerate -- --no-sync
git add asyncapi.yaml asyncapi.public.yaml

npm run complete:light
